From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: theycallmeboxy <82409831+theycallmeboxy@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 20:29:48 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] panvk: allocate ms2ss images' memory on first use

An image created with VK_IMAGE_CREATE_MULTISAMPLED_RENDER_TO_SINGLE_SAMPLED_BIT_EXT
gets a hidden multisampled image for every supported sample count (4x, 8x and
16x on Mali-G615), and their sizes were added to the image's memory
requirements and bound into the application's memory. Such an image cost
1 + 4 + 8 + 16 = 29 times its single-sampled size, whether or not it was
ever rendered to with multisampling.

Zink sets the flag on every colour-renderable image when the extension is
available, so OpenGL games through Zink paid it on most of their textures:
DOOM 3 BFG grew to 4 GB of GPU memory (1.2 GB with the extension hidden; the
stock Mali driver, which also exposes the extension, uses 0.8 GB).

Report and bind only the single-sampled image. A multisampled image gets its
own driver-owned memory the first time a render pass uses that sample count
with ms2ss, and its view is created then too (views bake image addresses into
their descriptors). Both are serialized by a lock. If the allocation fails,
the command buffer fails with VK_ERROR_OUT_OF_DEVICE_MEMORY. The memory is
freed with the image.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QAYrqSPd4TgpVaKLqz5cYR
(cherry picked from commit 50874a212f26bd87e20afedae36d61a135a0a7bb)

Purpose: stop VK_EXT_multisampled_render_to_single_sampled images from reserving 2x/4x/8x/16x multisampled copies up front (29x the image's size on Mali-G615); Zink sets the flag on every colour-renderable image, so OpenGL games through Zink ran out of GPU memory (DOOM 3 BFG 4 GB, Jupiter Hell 4.2 GB while loading)
Upstream-commit: none (Mesa main has the same eager allocation; upstream candidate)
Tested GPU: Mali-G615 MC6 (Anbernic RG477M, Dimensity 8300, v11)
Tested Kbase UAPI: CSF 1.21 / MediaTek
Dependencies: none of ours; applies on the full g615-v11-csf series
Validation test: msrtss (64x64 RGBA8 ms2ss image; clear+draw at 4x, load+draw at 8x, load+blend at 16x, average resolve): identical pixels to the unpatched driver, edge pixels blended, 20 create/use/destroy loops stable; memory requirement 468 KiB -> 20 KiB. DOOM 3 BFG peak GPU memory 4073 -> 1237 MB, Jupiter Hell 4.2 GB (cap) -> 1022 MB; drawbench checksums 8/8 and racetest identical
